Falsifies `kernel::sched::tests::binding_to_an_interrupt_refuses_a_parked_sender`.

The defect: `refuse_parked_sender` marks the parked sender refused and never wakes it. The queue
is empty, so no receive collects the sender's words, but the sender sleeps for ever on a send
that will never complete. It is the half of the fix a reader who only wanted the driver
protected would write.

Expected to fail: "the bind left the parked sender asleep", because nothing wakes the sender.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched/interrupt_route.rs b/kernel/src/sched/interrupt_route.rs
index df95d0076..8e12781aa 100644
--- a/kernel/src/sched/interrupt_route.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched/interrupt_route.rs
@@ -75,7 +75,6 @@ fn refuse_parked_sender(sched: &mut IpcTables, tid: ThreadId) {
     }
     set_ipc_aborted(sched, tid);
     set_ipc_refused(sched, tid);
-    wake(sched, tid);
 }
 
 /// The rendezvous an interrupt is routed to, if any. Read from the interrupt handler; lock-free.
